WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.360
This is a pot of cool water.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.530
And this is a pot of boiling water.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.300
We've all heard the analogy.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.463
Place a frog in the boiling
water, and he'll jump right out.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.130
But place him in the cool water

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.300
and slowly bring the water to boil

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.203
and the frog won't know he's
boiling till it's too late.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.910
And that in a nutshell is
modern American policing.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.138
It's how we got from here.

00:00:28.138 --> 00:00:29.988
Put on his new uniform.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:31.973
To here.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.883
Now this did not happen overnight.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.710
A series of major historical
events transpired.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.350
Laws were passed and decades
of slow cultural shift

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.000
brought us to this boiling point.

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:56.410
They are literally pointing guns.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.250
And now that we're in the hot water,

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.913
the question is, how do you jump out?

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.300
This is professor Peter B. Kraska.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.910
He wrote one of the most
popular incited studies

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.330
on police militarization.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.690
Militarism is basically at its heart,

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.250
a problem solving ideology.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.760
It says that the best
way to solve problems

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.560
that you have in front
of you is to use violence

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.560
and military type weaponry and
the threat of that violence

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.287
to solve the problem.

00:01:36.287 --> 00:01:39.237
And that's what we're saying
in today's police institution.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.300
Generally speaking police militarization

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.270
has been seen as a problem
in developing nations,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.090
but concern has increasingly
turned to the United States

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.683
on both sides of the aisle.

00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:55.210
Here's a massive study done by
none other than Charles Koch

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.030
of the Koch Brothers about this very topic

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.823
and why we should all be concerned.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.133
But this is not an
exclusively modern problem.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.230
Its roots can be traced all the way back

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.693
to the original colonies.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.640
The earliest form of policing
in America was slave patrols.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.910
The first of which were
established in 1704.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.970
This is historian and author
professor Sally Hadden.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.390
The slave patrols are

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.330
what we might think of as pre-policing.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:32.970
Their job was a combination
of social control

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.700
and racial control to
try to enforce the norms

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.910
that the white community
wanted to see in place.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.910
They were created to try to
restrain slaves from behaviors

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.160
that the white community
did not approve of.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.246
They had guns, they had
dogs, they had whips.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.270
Once slavery was ended across the South,

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.337
slave patrols were effectively replaced

00:03:05.337 --> 00:03:09.460
by white community leaders
with either police forces

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.820
or a little bit later
with vigilante groups,

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.333
such as the KU Klux Klan.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.370
Northern troops were often tasked

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.470
with policing Southern states
during the Reconstruction Era

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.270
and president Rutherford B. Hayes

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.340
was accused of using the
military as a political tool

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.113
to bust unions, sway elections
and quell civil unrest.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.800
Scores of protestors
were killed and injured

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.583
during the Great Railroad Strike of 1877.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:43.100
The following year Congress
passed the Posse Comitatus Act,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.150
making it illegal to use
any part of the US military

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.363
as law enforcement.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.680
How many people are talking
about Posse Comitatus anymore?

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.860
It's very irrelevant.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.360
If someone cares about
one of the key tenants

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.970
of democratic governance
is a clear distinction

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.103
between the military, which
focuses on external threats

00:04:03.103 --> 00:04:07.550
and the police, which serves
the democratic citizenry

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.600
of the United States and have a bright

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.173
clear line between those.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.940
That bright clear line

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:17.690
blurred gradually over the
course of three American Wars,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.313
not those three, these three.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.120
The first point of the frog being boiled

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.710
was the social unrest of the 1960s.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.210
As a response to growing
inner city violence,

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.970
President Lyndon Johnson
declared a war on crime

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.623
and signed the Law Enforcement
Assistance Act in 1965.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.450
A $30 million program
provided police departments

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:44.040
across the country with
bulletproof vests, helicopters,

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.053
tanks, rifles, gas masks,
and other tactical gear.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.500
Less than one month later, the
Watts riots shocked America

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.463
and left 34 people dead.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.210
Los Angeles Police,
chief William H. Parker

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.630
characterize the riots as an insurgency

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:07.850
and to create a paramilitary
response to the disorder.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.070
14,000 national guardsmen
joined the police

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.160
in trying to maintain
order on the streets.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.230
Three years later,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.300
the country was in a
state of complete turmoil.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.910
Martin Luther King was shot

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:20.981
and was killed tonight.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.070
The assassination of
Martin Luther King Jr.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.900
triggered riots across
major cities in America,

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.603
especially in Chicago.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.410
The show of force was staggering,

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:38.770
10,500 police, over 6,700
national guard troops

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.090
and 5,000 soldiers from the 1st Armored

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.990
and 5th Infantry divisions
patrolled the streets.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:44.823
President Jonathan

00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:46.170
declared a state of emergency.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.190
That declaration resulted in
the virtually unthinkable act

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.300
of regular army troops deployed

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.950
to protect the Capitol
and the White House.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.170
Just a few months later

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.420
after the assassination of Bobby Kennedy,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.150
protestors clashed
violently with police forces

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.330
during the Democratic National Convention.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.263
And all of it was televised.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.090
It was over this tumultuous
period that SWAT teams

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:14.020
were first formed as part
of a larger police effort

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.290
to militarize responses to riots

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.910
and other types of civil unrest.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.200
Even though that was its genesis,

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.300
the real cause of today's
police militarization

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.990
was the Reagan, Bush and
then Clinton drug wars.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.750
I believe this program will prove

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.781
to be a highly effective
attack on drug trafficking.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.190
In 1981, president Ronald Reagan

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:37.890
signed the military cooperation

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.473
with Civilian Law
Enforcement Agencies Act.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.060
The line between the
military and law enforcement

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.280
continued to blur as police forces

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.470
received increasing monetary
and tactical assistance,

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.290
and for the first time SWAT teams

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.503
became a regular part of
law enforcement operations.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.840
Decade later, as the drug wars dragged on

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.740
with no victory in sight,
president George Walker Bush

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:04.570
launched the 1033 Program.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.290
This cleared a frictionless path

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.410
for the Department of Defense

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.770
to issue massive amounts of military gear

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:12.663
and battlefield weaponry
to local law enforcement.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.490
It's worth noting that all
this gear was and remains

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.900
to this day free to any police department

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.450
that takes part in the program.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:23.103
All they have to do is
pay for shipping costs.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.420
Let us roll up our sleeves to roll back

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.830
this awful tide of violence and
reduce crime in our country.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:32.960
The Clinton administration

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.000
expanded the 1033 Program

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.480
after a North Hollywood
bank robbery in 1997.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:40.440
The two bank robbers dressed in

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:44.270
heavy body armor and carrying
automatic assault rifles,

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.250
simply outgunned the LAPD.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.750
This coupled with incidents

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:50.230
like the Columbine shooting

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.380
and escalated gun violence all around,

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.640
made it painfully clear
that the police needed

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.890
to be better prepared for the type of arms

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:59.413
that the general public
had easy access to.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.960
We have seen in the last 25 years,

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.263
an internal arms race.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.900
We've seen the police arming themselves

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:15.823
and the people arming themselves
at an unprecedented level.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.757
The first plane hit the first

00:08:18.757 --> 00:08:20.380
of the World Trade Center towers

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.912
at 8:50 thereabouts Eastern Time.

00:08:23.912 --> 00:08:26.440
One World Trade Center has collapsed

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.190
in its entirety.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.580
One World Trade Center is gone.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.330
The second tower just collapsed.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.080
We will work closely with our coalition

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.730
to deny terrorists and their
state sponsors the materials,

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.970
technology, and expertise
to make and deliver

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:45.633
weapons of mass destruction.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:50.210
The war on terror really
created a new environment

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:54.710
for policing, where there
was this tangible threat

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.490
that they had to be aware of.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:09:00.290
And so under the auspices
of preparing for terrorism,

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:05.160
we saw a real acceleration
of police militarization.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.640
You had all of these police officers

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.820
going through training camps,
for-profit training camps

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:15.820
funded by DOJ and DHS and
getting this weaponry.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.990
Since 1990, law enforcement agencies

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.470
have received over $6
billion in military hardware

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.790
from the Department of Defense.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.790
Between 2006 and 2014
alone, the DOD transferred

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.400
600 mine-resistant armored vehicles,

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:36.400
79,288 assault rifles,
205 grenade launchers,

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.650
almost 12,000 bayonets, 50 airplanes,

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:44.650
422 helicopters and $3.6 million
with the tactical clothing

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.420
to 80% of all the nations
local law enforcement offices.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.560
Much of this arsenal
was transferred directly

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.260
from the middle East
into us police precincts,

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.530
especially after 2011 when
president Barack Obama

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.373
began pulling troops out of Iraq.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.620
And now you see police on a

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:08.010
to wear full battle dress utilities,

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:11.960
to pursue problems with
the militaristic approach,

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.530
go into neighborhoods and occupy them

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:18.086
as if they're doing some
sort of counterinsurgency

00:10:18.086 --> 00:10:21.023
and fully embrace the military model.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.900
And this brings us to an element perhaps

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.960
even more important than the gear,

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.560
it's best understood by applying

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.370
a classic psychological term

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.290
called the law of the instrument.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.310
So if you have a hammer in your hand,

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.383
everything begins to look like a nail.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:42.420
Police departments have the
technology of a SWAT team.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.623
They have the armament of the military.

00:10:45.508 --> 00:10:47.440
You're gonna want to use this stuff.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:50.050
It plays into warrior fantasies,

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:53.780
it gives it imagery
that's really intoxicating

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:56.813
to a segment of the police institution.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:59.360
What little data there is

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.010
supports these claims.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.840
SWAT style, no-knock raids,

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:06.123
have increased by 1400% since 1980.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.200
This is partly because SWAT
raids on low level offenders

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.930
are actually used as training exercises.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.640
But the key thing to remember,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.930
it's not the SWAT teams anymore,

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:20.210
it's how the ideology and the armament

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:24.490
and the tactical approach
has now dispersed

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.893
throughout the entire police institution.

00:11:30.128 --> 00:11:33.557
Don't shoot, don't shoot,

00:11:33.557 --> 00:11:35.460
don't shoot, don't shoot.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.120
Reaction to the grand jury's decision

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.950
left destruction in the street
of Ferguson this morning.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.120
The grand jury decided

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.640
not to charge officer Darren Wilson

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.655
and the shooting death of Michael Brown.

00:11:45.655 --> 00:11:48.861
Don't shoot, don't shoot,

00:11:48.861 --> 00:11:49.861
don't shoot.

00:11:53.321 --> 00:11:55.238
Move, move!

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.910
It wasn't until Ferguson that

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.900
the rest of the United States
of America finally woke up

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.810
to the kinds of things that
were going on at policing.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.883
So it came to a boiling point.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.360
In response to Ferguson,
president Barack Obama

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.510
issued an audit of American policing

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:19.490
and signing executive order
scaling back the 1033 Program.

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:22.670
We've seen how militarized gear

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.430
can sometimes give people a feeling like

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:29.330
there's an occupying force
as opposed to a force

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:30.700
that's part of the community

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.700
that's protecting them and serving them.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.340
But his actions did nothing

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:38.800
to curb the myriad other means
of acquiring tactical gear,

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.790
nor did it address the larger problem

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.090
of militarized police culture.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.000
And what little Obama may
have accomplished was reversed

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.500
two years later when attorney
general Jeff Sessions

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.340
on behalf of president Donald Trump

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.064
lifted the executive order.

00:12:52.064 --> 00:12:55.667
He's resending restrictions
from the prior administration

00:12:55.667 --> 00:12:59.980
that limited your agency's
ability to get equipment

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:03.483
through federal programs,
including lifesaving gear.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.240
Which pretty much brings us to today.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.130
I can't breath .

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.420
George Floyd's killing at the hands

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:20.265
of the Minneapolis Police
Department prompted mass protest.

00:13:20.265 --> 00:13:22.740
We don't need more violence.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.157
Move!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.380
Calls for reform from
reducing police funding

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.430
to disbanding precincts altogether

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.763
became rallying cries nationwide.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.380
I took the helmet off
and laid the batons down.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:10.040
Public pressure has moved the needle

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.570
on this issue, and cities
like Camden, New Jersey

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.720
have become representative

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:16.203
of a new community focused policing model.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:20.320
But across the nation,
the dice remains cast,

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:23.660
and president Trump has taken
a decidedly divisive approach

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:24.493
on the matter.

00:14:24.493 --> 00:14:29.260
June 1st finally gave us a hallmark moment

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:34.130
to really demonstrate the
unequivocal support Trump

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:36.563
has been giving police militarization.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.560
Tensions only escalated
after Trump's follow up

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:44.150
and the assault by soldiers
on peaceful protestors.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.420
At the behest of attorney
general, William Barr,

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:49.470
Portland, Oregon was flooded
with unidentified forces

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:50.587
dressed as soldiers.

00:14:50.587 --> 00:14:52.320
[Female protestor] What is going on?

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.710
Who are you?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.160
Detaining demonstrators
in unmarked vehicles,

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.723
and even assaulting peaceful protestors.

00:14:59.791 --> 00:15:02.480
This is why I pay tax.
Move, move.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.370
Lawsuits have already been filed

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.900
over these arguably
shocking acts of violence

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.250
by federal agents against
American citizens.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.730
But that hasn't stopped
president Trump from threatening

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:16.000
further federal deployments
to other major cities,

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.480
escalating tensions between police forces

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.006
and the citizens they're supposed to.

00:15:21.006 --> 00:15:23.186
If you don't move, you will be dead.

00:15:23.186 --> 00:15:24.700
Move out of the way.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.820
The frog is boiled, it's not even notice,

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.150
the police wouldn't even recognize

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.360
the word police militarization,

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:36.750
because it's just something
they are part of and live with,

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.590
and they really do scratch
their head often times

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.090
as to where this critical
thinking is coming from.

